The '''Ring of Kafrene''', also referred to simply as '''Kafrene''', was a [[mining]] colony and deep-[[Realspace|space]] trading post in the [[Kafrene asteroid belt]] of the [[Thand sector]]. During the [[Galactic Civil War]], the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] [[Mission to the Ring of Kafrene|sent]] intelligence [[agent]] [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] here prior to the [[Battle of Scarif]]. There, Andor confirmed the existence of the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]].

==Characteristics==
[[File:Kafrene-City.jpg|thumb|left|250px|The interior cityscape of the Ring of Kafrene]]
The Ring of Kafrene was a monumental construction which served as both a mining colony and a deep-space trading post. Its structures, made from [[durasteel]] and [[plastoid]], were slung between a pair of malformed [[planetoid]]s in the [[Kafrene asteroid belt]]. Areas such as its aft [[Hangar|docking bay]] were covered in lurid, phosphorescent graffiti. Roads led out from the docking bays towards the distant rock warrens of the planetoids, and the outpost itself was a labyrinthine sprawl of shacks, prefabricated housing, and countless maze-like corridors. Although there was some structure to the buildings around the main throughways, beyond these areas the layout of the Ring changed almost daily; shacks were made of sheet metal, and shelters utilized housing units recycled from foreign colonies. [[Alien]] housing complexes and tenements featured ventilation shafts that sent wafts of [[ammonia]] into the streets.<ref name="RO novel" /> The Ring acted as a junction between the [[Corellian Trade Spine]]&mdash;which connected it to the [[planet]]s [[Coruscant]] and [[Anoat]]&mdash;and the [[Biox Detour]], which connected it to the planets [[Takodana]] and [[Malastare]].<ref name="Smuggler's Guide">''[[Star Wars: Smuggler's Guide]]''</ref>

==History==
[[File:MissiontoKafrene.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Cassian Andor and Tivik meeting on the Ring of Kafrene]]
The Ring of Kafrene was constructed by members of [[Noble|nobility]] in the [[Galactic Republic]], and was established as a mining colony to strip the [[asteroid]]s and [[planetoid]]s of the [[Kafrene asteroid belt]] of any valuable minerals. However, the founders soon realized that such coveted minerals were scarce in the Kafrene belt, and the failed mining venture became a trading post and stopover point for desperate travelers<ref name="RO novel" /> through the [[Thand sector]].<ref name="RO World Locations" /> The covert special forces group [[Zero Company]] were headquartered at Kafrene during the [[Clone Wars]], operating from a base known as [[Den (Ring of Kafrene)|The Den]].<ref name="Zero Company Join the Ranks" />

The [[Galactic Empire]] maintained a presence on Kafrene, and Imperial [[stormtrooper]]s patrolled its streets. Prior to the [[Liberation of Erso]] on [[Wobani]], the [[Alliance to Restore the Republic]] sent [[Cassian Jeron Andor|Cassian Andor]] to the Ring of Kafrene<ref name="Rogue One" /> to investigate why Imperial shipments of [[kyber crystal]]s were being shipped across [[the galaxy]].<ref name="Rebel Dossier">''[[Star Wars: Rogue One: Rebel Dossier]]''</ref> In [[section nine]], Cassian met with [[Tivik]], an informant who revealed the existence of a "planet-killer"&ndash;truly the [[DS-1 Orbital Battle Station|Death Star]]&ndash;before [[stormtrooper]]s accosted the pair. Cassian shot them down, then killed Tivik when he proved a liability, before fleeing the area.<ref name="Rogue One" />

[[File:FalconLeavesKafrene-2015StarWars50.jpg|thumb|left|250px|Han Solo leaves the Ring of Kafrene]]
At the same [[time]] as the Rebel Alliance celebrated their [[Rebel Alliance Navy|fleet]] on the [[Mako-Ta Space Docks]], [[Han Solo]] was on the Ring of Kafrene with [[Chewbacca]] and [[C-3PO]], where he made a deal with an [[Alaphani]] for a set of [[transponder code]]s. After Chewbacca noticed a pair of [[bounty hunter]]s watching them, Solo finished the deal, giving the Alaphani [[credit chip]]s in exchange for the codes. The two bounty hunters followed them, but were ambushed by Solo, who took their weapons and promised them that [[Jabba Desilijic Tiure|Jabba]] would get his money. They boarded the ''[[Millennium Falcon]]'' and left the Ring of Kafrene,<ref name="Star Wars 50">[[Star Wars (2015) 50|''Star Wars'' (2015) 50]]</ref> returning to Mako-Ta to discover that it was [[Battle of Mako-Ta|under attack]] by [[Anakin Skywalker|Darth Vader]] and his [[Death Squadron]].<ref name="Star Wars 51">[[Star Wars (2015) 51|''Star Wars'' (2015) 51]]</ref> After escaping the attack, he sold the data that he got from the Ring of Kafrene to [[Sana Starros]] on [[Nar Shaddaa]].<ref name="Star Wars 55">[[Star Wars (2015) 55|''Star Wars'' (2015) 55]]</ref>

[[0-0-0]] and [[BT-1]] were picked up by Imperials during a sweep of the Ring of Kafrene. They were fitted with restraining bolts and returned to service.<ref name="Aphra38">[[Doctor Aphra (2016) 38|''Doctor Aphra'' (2016) 38]]</ref>

==Inhabitants==
[[File:Kafrene-Streets.jpg|thumb|right|250px|The crowded streetways of the Ring hosted a plethora of individuals]]
As a deep-space trading outpost and stopover point for travelers, the Ring of Kafrene hosted crowds of individuals including [[human]]s, [[Alien|nonhumans]], and beings of indeterminate [[gender]]s. Many of these became stuck on the outpost, sentenced to live among the pressing crowds with a characteristic plodding gait. Workers toiled during the day, and stuck to the main throughways at night due to the constantly shifting nature of the Ring's layout.<ref name="RO novel" />

==Behind the scenes==
According to [[Tony Gilroy]], the name "Kafrene" originated from how Gilroy's daughter Kathryn used to call herself when younger.<ref name="StarWarsExplained">{{YouTube|video=lfxF5ezrRDo|text=Tony Gilroy On Andor And His Advice For The Future Of Star Wars|channel=@StarWarsExplained|name=Star Wars Explained|date=2025-06-13}} </ref>

